 "date_and_limits": [
  "2016 July 1 publication date for Gao Can 88, not a verified exposure date. The native 3083×2074 original resolves two vertical glazing bars, the low door sill and terrace glazing. Only the number, arch and masonry are used as historic-to-current identity evidence.",
  "The 2023 hedge masks the near ground and some low panes. The older glazed rooftop enclosure is omitted from the 2023 state. The commercial signs, umbrellas, and garden furniture are not projected onto the building. On the north porch only the stationary blind case is modeled.",
  "Three complete fitting stations for the lawn gable are independent of the number-wing/porch material targets. The near view (12) is geometrically transferred using the actual numbered brick plane; the foreground glass depth is less certain there.",
  "The floor, copings, side wing returns and rear cut are estimates. The exterior toe of the segmental opening, its broad pale ring, the brass number, two gable elevations, lawn terrace and north angled sides appear in the source views. The strict material tests retain any imperfect edge hits and later garden planting as separate observations."
 ],
